  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed an intimate eleven-song set for KEXP Radio on Friday, May 29, 2015 [1][2]. This session marks the 206th archived show for the band, following a performance at the Urban Lounge just two days earlier [2]. The setlist features a mix of well-known tracks and deeper cuts, with three songs experiencing long gaps in the archive before this date [2]. “Some Swedish Trees” returned after a 2,415-day absence, while “Isaiah 45:23” appeared after a 2,004-day hiatus, making it a rare entry with only thirteen archived performances [2]. “Michael Myers Resplendent” also saw a significant gap of 1,071 days [2]. The remaining songs, including “Island Garden Song,” “Jaipur,” “Woke Up New,” “Animal Mask,” “Love Cuts the Strings,” “Steal Smoked Fish,” “Cry for Judas,” and “Up the Wolves,” rounded out the program [1][2]. The band shared spoken introductions and stories about banter, “Animal Mask,” and a pick [1]. The recommended recording is a 35-minute FLAC file captured from the KEXP web stream [1]. The uploader noted that the audio is amplified and tracked in Audacity, with a brief skip near the end of “Isaiah 45:23” and slightly quiet levels on the opening track [1]. This file is the only available recording of the event, offering a complete view of the session [1][2].",
